--- kps-S31ah k-dependence finding ---
The Lee-Yang/phi^4 lambda-frame TRACKS consec-max EXACTLY: consec IS the lambda-argmin through k=11
(k=8,9,10,11 True) and STOPS being it at k=12,13 (False) -- the SAME k=12 breakdown as consec-max
(HYP-2780). corr(lambda, cap-q0) peaks +0.895 at k=11, declines to +0.825 at k=13. So the Lee-Yang
extremality is a REPARAMETRIZATION of the coverage extremality (same binding rows, same k=12 break),
NOT an independent bypass. It IS the right object for the BINDING rows k=8,9,10 (consec=lambda-argmin,
corr +0.86-0.90), where the cap is tight. At k>=12 the cap is loose (gap +0.23,+0.32) so the break
doesn't matter. CONCLUSION: the phi^4/Lee-Yang frame is the correct geometric picture of the binding-row
coverage extremality; the Asano-monotonicity proof lever applies to k=8,9,10 specifically.
